| `scripts/module_identity.py` | Registers a script under its sibling and package import names so its classes and state have one identity. Binds the module on the matching `scripts` package. | imported; `register_module(__name__, __file__)` | — | Stdlib-only and 3.6-safe. Requires a `sys.modules` entry before execution. Leaves a different `scripts` package alone. Not for configuration reads: `scripts/config_loader.py` owns those. | [python-style.md](../guides/python-style.md) | always |
